<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  Password overlay for the e2e ClickHouse container.

  The shipped docker/clickhouse/users.xml ships the literal placeholder
  CHANGE_ME_GENERATE_SECURE_PASSWORD; install.sh sed-replaces it at install
  time, and CI never runs install.sh — which is exactly why the E2E job has
  been failing since ClickHouse started rejecting the placeholder login.

  Rather than mutating a tracked repo file (and leaving a dirty working tree
  when a run is killed), this file is mounted as an ADDITIONAL users.d entry.
  ClickHouse merges users.d/*.xml in filename order, so "users-e2e.xml" is
  applied after "custom.xml" and only the <password> nodes are overridden —
  the profiles, quotas and network ACLs from the shipped file still apply, so
  the e2e run keeps exercising the real configuration.

  __CH_PASSWORD__ is substituted by web/e2e/stack/up.sh from e2e.env.

  ===========================================================================
  Do NOT add a <default> user here (issue #70).

  The image entrypoint owns `default`: it writes users.d/default-user.xml with
      <password><![CDATA[$CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD]]></password>
  and "default-user.xml" sorts BEFORE "users-e2e.xml", so anything we declare
  for <default> merges on top of that CDATA node. ClickHouse's config merge
  only REPLACES an existing text child when it is a TEXT node; a CDATA_SECTION
  node is a different node type, so the incoming text is APPENDED instead and
  the effective password becomes the value twice over:
      <password><![CDATA[secret]]>secret</password>   ->  "secretsecret"
  The entrypoint's own init client then authenticates with "secret", gets
  Code: 516 AUTHENTICATION_FAILED, and the container dies mid-`CREATE DATABASE`
  on FIRST boot only. `restart: unless-stopped` brings it back, boot two skips
  init because the data dir now exists, and it goes healthy — which is why this
  looked like a slow/flaky cold start rather than a crash.

  `purl` is safe to declare: the entrypoint never touches it, so this merges
  TEXT-onto-TEXT into the placeholder in docker/clickhouse/users.xml.
-->
<clickhouse>
    <users>
        <purl>
            <password>__CH_PASSWORD__</password>
        </purl>
    </users>
</clickhouse>
